Package: popburden
Title: Reconcile Multi-Source Estimates into Patient Population and Disease Burden Figures
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Muhammad", "Zia ul Haq", email = "muhammad.zia@fulbrightmail.org",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0338-9552"))
Description: Tools for turning imperfect, heterogeneous epidemiological
    inputs -- survey-based prevalence, registry counts, model-based
    estimates -- into a single decision-ready patient population or
    disease burden figure. Implements inverse-variance and
    DerSimonian-Laird random-effects reconciliation of independent
    source estimates, direct age standardization with a Poisson
    parametric-bootstrap confidence interval for small counts, Monte
    Carlo conversion of a rate into an absolute patient count under a
    normal, log-normal, or beta sampling distribution, and a simple
    demographic-driven forward projection for multi-year forecasting.
    Every numeric routine ships with a closed-form or simulation-based
    uncertainty estimate; none silently drop the confidence interval.
